18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":8,"created_at":"2025-05-05T16:32:01Z","updated_at":"2025-06-08T22:51:32Z","closed_at":"2025-06-08T22:51:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5-dev3 and current master [1cf573f44de045ee73fd938fbf2bdccc0e31b7bb]\n- Not reproducible in 4.5-dev2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev.mono (d2964eab7) - Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS 24.04 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV RENOIR) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a non-looping animation is played in the editor, it 'jumps' to the beginning of the animation and sets the animated properties to the average? of the start and end values (I haven't tested this in detail - so it might be different for different animated tracks/properties).\nIt does only happen in the editor, not in the running game.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe mrp contains an animation that moves a `Sprite2D` from `(10, 0)` to `(100, 0)`. When the animation is played in the editor, the timeline-cursor jumps to the start and sets the position to `(55, 0)` when it's finished.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20040295/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/us